    "scope": "For each fixed degree d>=5, retain full deep-triple tensor comparison and closed-corner intrinsic/protected-ambient GH collapse with O(log R/R) distortion. Add explicit projective normal-bundle coordinates on fixed source-free base domains, canonical global primitives and moments, and a uniform averaged moment interval from fixed-end convergence. Add exact staged circle averaging, all marked-period transport, Hamiltonian comparison of averaging paths and integer bases, and an adapted closed-corner bundle with the same GH rate. Distinguish bounded neck volume envelopes from tensor asymptotics; give a residual-boundary counterexample, a mixed-coefficient rank-one circle criterion, and conditional coupled-background and complete-product identification. Full-neck flow buffers, simultaneous triple-end action/reduced-foliation matching, sources and global GH remain open. Novelty is unconfirmed.",
    "verification": "New proofs independently read, with primary-source checks of Song Definition 2.3 and Lemmas 4.4-4.5, Rochon-Zhang equations (5.5)-(5.6) and Theorem 5.1, Zhang Lemma 3.3, Mandel section 2.3, and the Laplacian maximum principle. Audited explicit inverse coordinates, period-one normalization, fixed-end limit order, staged exact transport, Hamiltonian path/image buffers, C1/Gronwall GH transfer, residual counterexample and determinant criterion. Recursive inputs, labels, references, citations, braces, environments and introduced macros checked; optional local-font input remains optional. Current revised PDFs have not been compiled because lualatex.fmt and LuaTeX-ja assets are unavailable. No formal verification, comprehensive novelty audit or fresh audit of all older global constructions is claimed."
